3	// ============================================================================
4	// prodigy_sm90.cuh — CANONICAL SuperGrok sm_90 device kernels for 'prodigy'.
5	//
6	// This header is the SINGLE source of truth for the sm_90 device logic:
7	// templated __forceinline__ __device__ update/_vec4 functions, the __global__
8	// launcher kernels, every inline-PTX (asm-volatile) block VERBATIM, and (for
9	// muon/supergrok2) the CUTLASS Sm90 tensor-core collectives. It is a
10	// composition primitive for the future fused megakernel.
11	//
12	// The production TU csrc/backends/cuda/sm_90/launch_prodigy.cu now #include's
13	// this header and keeps only the host launcher(s) the pybind layer calls.
14	// Migrated byte-for-byte from that .cu; verified compile-neutral via the
15	// preprocessor-equivalence gate (nvcc -E, modulo __FILE__).
16	// ============================================================================
17	// CUDA sm_90 launch glue for Prodigy.
18	// Algorithm: csrc/algorithms/prodigy.h
19	//
20	// Three-kernel orchestration:
21	//   (1) reduce  — block-reduce (r, s) partial sums
22	//   (2) update  — single-thread d update
23	//   (3) apply   — Adam with d as effective learning rate
24	// All on-device; d_t never round-trips through CPU.
